26                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         About LAWA\n\n
27  Land, Air, Water Aotearoa (LAWA) has been established by like-minded organisations with a view to helping local communities find the balance between using natural resources and maintaining their quality and availability.  LAWA connects us with the environment by sharing environmental data and information.   Initially a collaboration between New Zealand’s 16 regional councils and unitary authorities, LAWA is now a partnership between the Te Uru Kahika - Regional and Unitary Councils Aotearoa, Cawthron Institute, the Ministry for the Environment, the Department of Conservation, Statistics New Zealand and has been supported by the Tindall Foundation and Massey University.

